ISO-10303-21;
/* M066: Non-manifold COMPSOLID translated as a set of independent SOLIDs; input: AP214 STEP file (OCCT STEPControl_ActorWrite.cxx:992 pattern) with two MANIFOLD_SOLID_BREPs whose CLOSED_SHELLs each reference the same shared ADVANCED_FACE entity (face #shared_face); on non-manifold COMPSOLID round-trip the shared face is duplicated and the cellular/shared-face topology is lost; OCCT STEPControl_ActorWrite.cxx:992 comment: 'NonManifold COMPSOLID was translated like a set of SOLIDs'; kernel must heal and accept: preserve compsolid via SHELL_BASED_SURFACE_MODEL or AP242 non-manifold subtypes; warn-and-accept if the AP does not support it; synonyms: compsolid decomposed, non-manifold lost on write, shared face topology dropped, COMPSOLID broken into independent solids */
